# Cesare throws the reversing lever and the blocked capsule comes out on Lino's
# side. The payoff of the prototype's whole chain.
#
# The flag is third and not last on purpose: it is what the lever's StateVisual
# watches, so raising it here is what drops the knob into its notch on the clack
# rather than after the closing line. It does not change the meaning — the line
# reverses when the lever is thrown, not when the narrator has finished saying
# so — and it is safe because sequence_if is checked before the scene starts, so
# raising it half way cancels nothing.

uid baggaseqleve01

say   SEQ_LEVER_PULL
sound sfx_lever_throw
flag  line_reversed

sound hum_low
say   SEQ_LEVER_RUMBLE

# The wait is the silence the closing line describes; the thud arrives while it
# is still ringing.
wait  0.8
sound sfx_capsule_land_far
say   SEQ_LEVER_END
